 "result": "csvsum.py reads stdin as bytes, splits on newlines, skips the header and short or blank rows, groups float values by category in a dict, then prints each category's math.fsum total with %.2f in sorted order. It passes the public sample (in-0/out-0) and is registered by assay at 1.89004 (noise 3.1%). The one variant I tried (drop the per-line empty check, fewer ops per row) scored 1.871 against an incumbent of 1.872, so it was not adopted. I'm resting because the remaining per-row cost is mostly float parsing and the Python loop, and further gains look smaller than the 3.1% noise floor.",
